      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cast equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has a yield strength of 163–530 MPa at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::001::introduction::0f933d56a0",
        "PMC7513042::chunk::001::introduction::f13797f6f6"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has inadequate resistance to oxidation in high-temperature air.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::chunk::001::introduction::f13797f6f6"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr suffers pesting during high-temperature air exposure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to introduce approximately 3 at.% Al into equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr during arc melting.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 3 at.% Al will preferentially oxidize during high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 3 at.% Al will produce a continuous, adherent, and dense Al2O3 surface scale on HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Al2O3 scale will act as a barrier to oxygen diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Restricting oxygen diffusion through the Al2O3 scale will retard oxidation and pesting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr, the Al-modified alloy will have significantly lower oxidation weight gain after 5 hours in air at 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will not undergo pesting during a 5-hour exposure to air at 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain room-temperature tensile ductility within the 8–16% range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain high-temperature yield strength similar to untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed oxidation-resistance effect is bounded to air at 800 °C for exposures of up to 5 hours.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanical-performance boundary covers temperatures up to 1000 °C and strain rates of 10^-4–10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The adhesion and uniformity of an alumina scale formed by 3 at.% Al, and the resulting changes in mechanical properties, remain uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
